@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Research — go-multipackage (example.com/checkout)
+
+## Units under test
+- `money.Discount(subtotalCents, percent)` — returns the discount amount in cents;
+  rejects a negative subtotal and a percent outside `0..100`; integer division truncates.
+- `shipping.Rate(weightGrams, brackets)` — first bracket whose `UpToGrams >= weight`
+  wins (equality belongs to that bracket); rejects a negative weight and empty brackets;
+  weight above every bracket falls back to the last bracket.
+- `order.Total(subtotal, weight, discountPolicy, shippingCalculator)` — composes
+  `subtotal - discount + shipping`; validates the subtotal first, then calls the
+  discount policy, then the shipping calculator, propagating the first error.
+
+## Collaborators
+`order` depends on the `DiscountPolicy` and `ShippingCalculator` interfaces, so the
+composition and short-circuit behaviour can be driven with hand-written fakes that
+record call counts — no real money/shipping logic is needed.
+
+## Testability
+All three packages are pure and deterministic. Table-driven tests cover numeric
+boundaries; fakes cover the ordering guarantee that shipping is never consulted when
+the discount policy fails.
\ No newline at end of file
